## Prerequisites

- **PowerShell 7.0+** (cross-platform)
- **Pester 5.0+** for testing

### Install PowerShell 7+

**Windows:**
```powershell
winget install Microsoft.PowerShell
```

**macOS:**
```bash
brew install powershell
```

**Linux:**
```bash
# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y wget apt-transport-https software-properties-common
wget -q https://packages.microsoft.com/config/ubuntu/$(lsb_release -rs)/packages-microsoft-prod.deb
sudo dpkg -i packages-microsoft-prod.deb
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y powershell
```

### Install Pester

```powershell
Install-Module -Name Pester -MinimumVersion 5.0.0 -Force -SkipPublisherCheck
```

## Installation

```powershell
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/{{ author }}/{{ project_name }}.git
cd {{ project_name }}

# Import the module
Import-Module ./{{ project_name }}.psm1
```

## Usage

```powershell
# Example: Call the main function
Invoke-{{ project_name | replace('-', '') | title }}Function -Name "World"

# With pipeline
"PowerShell" | Invoke-{{ project_name | replace('-', '') | title }}Function

# With verbose output
Invoke-{{ project_name | replace('-', '') | title }}Function -Name "Test" -Verbose
```

## Development

### Run Tests

```powershell
# Run all tests
Invoke-Pester

# Run with coverage
Invoke-Pester -CodeCoverage {{ project_name }}.psm1

# Run specific test file
Invoke-Pester -Path ./{{ project_name }}.Tests.ps1
```

### Linting

```powershell
# Install PSScriptAnalyzer
Install-Module -Name PSScriptAnalyzer -Force -SkipPublisherCheck

# Run linter
Invoke-ScriptAnalyzer -Path . -Recurse
```

